---
/**
 * Privacy.
 *
 * This is a draft, and it says so at the top rather than in a comment.
 *
 * A privacy policy has to describe what a company actually does with
 * people's data, and only the company and its counsel can state that. What
 * this page can do honestly is describe what the marketing site itself does
 * today — which is verifiable, because it is this codebase — and mark
 * clearly which sections still need real text.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../data/company.js';
import { SITE_URL } from '../data/site.js';

const updated = 'not yet published';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Widgeta"
  description="How widgeta.app handles the information people give it, and what the site collects today."
  path="/privacy"
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="shell">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
  </div>

  <article class="doc">
    <p class="draft">
      <strong>Draft — not yet in force.</strong> The final policy has to be
      written and approved by Widgeta and its legal advisers before launch.
      What follows describes the marketing site as it is built today, and
      marks what still needs writing.
    </p>

    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="doc__meta muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>What this site collects today</h2>
    <p>
      widgeta.app is a set of static pages. It does not set cookies, it does
      not run analytics, and it loads no fonts, scripts or images from another
      company's servers — the typefaces are served from this site itself. If
      you only read these pages, nothing about you is recorded here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two forms exist. The "notify me" boxes on the home page, the pricing
      page and the call-answering page ask for an email address so we can tell
      you when that capability launches. The search box on the 404 page hands
      your words to Google, which is stated next to the box. Nothing else on
      this site asks you for anything.
    </p>
    <p class="todo">
      To write: where notify-me addresses are stored, who can read them, how
      long they are kept, and how to have one deleted. That copy cannot be
      accurate until the capture endpoint exists.
    </p>

    <h2>The application</h2>
    <p class="todo">
      To write: app.widgeta.app is a separate service that collects business
      details, photos and payment information. Its handling of that data,
      including processors, retention and international transfer, needs its
      own section written against how the product actually works.
    </p>

    <h2>Sites Widgeta builds for customers</h2>
    <p class="todo">
      To write: a Widgeta-generated site carries the customer's own business
      details and receives enquiries from the public. Who controls that data,
      and what happens to it when a customer cancels, belongs here.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p class="todo">
      To write: the rights available under GDPR, the UK GDPR, CCPA and Saudi
      and UAE data protection law, and how to exercise each of them — written
      against the markets Widgeta actually sells in.
    </p>

    <h2>Contacting us about privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> and a
      person answers within {CONTACT.responseWindow}.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-inline-size: var(--measure-narrow);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--s-4) var(--gutter) var(--section-y);
  }

  .draft {
    padding: var(--s-4);
    border: 2px dashed var(--soon-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    background: var(--soon-bg);
    color: var(--soon-text);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
  }

  .doc h1 { margin-block-start: var(--s-8); }

  .doc__meta { margin-block-start: var(--s-3); font-size: 14px; }

  .doc h2 {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-12);
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  }

  .doc p {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* An email address inside a sentence still gets tapped, so it gets a real
     target: padding rather than a taller line, so the paragraph keeps its
     rhythm. */
  .doc a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: 11px;
    color: var(--amber-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* An unwritten section is visibly unwritten. */
  .todo {
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--soon-line);
    background: var(--soon-bg);
    color: var(--soon-text) !important;
    font-size: 16px !important;
  }
</style>
